  "notes": "University Park track. Unlike the other Smeal majors, Actuarial Science starts directly with MATH 140/141 (Calc I/II) rather than MATH 110, and has its own heavy RM (Risk Management)/STAT sequence instead of the shared Smeal Year 3/4 core. The bulletin's 'select RM 412 or RM 422' requirement is simplified to just RM 422 (satisfiable a term earlier — RM 412 needs RM 411, completable only the same term as RM 422's slot). The 'select 3 credits from STAT 380/462/483' item lists STAT 483 first since it alone has no prerequisite (STAT 380/462 need STAT 200 specifically, which may not be the SCM 200/STAT 200 choice actually taken). 'etm' marks Smeal's Entrance-to-Major courses. For 2022-23, the RM/STAT sequence was structurally different: no RM 421/422 or MATH/STAT 415 at all — RM 411 and RM 412 (straight prescribed, not an elective pair) replace them, STAT 414 stood alone (not cross-listed with MATH), and the Additional Courses were RM 401-or-420 and RM 415-or-STAT 483 instead of the current elective pools. RM 401 is listed first since RM 420 needs RM 412, which is not yet done when this slot is reached. Post-parens-fix re-scrape (AND/OR prereq-parsing bug fix) revealed two real, previously-hidden gaps, same as ACTSC-2026.json: (1) ACCTG 211 and SCM 200 both need MATH 21, itself needing MATH 4, itself needing MATH 3 — none were in the plan, permanently blocking ACCTG 211/SCM 200 and everything downstream. Added the real chain explicitly: MATH 3 (Semester 1), MATH 4 (Semester 2), MATH 21 (Semester 3). (2) BLAW 341/BA 342 and BA 411 both require BA 302 or SCM 301 in one of their AND-groups — neither was anywhere in the plan. Added SCM 301 explicitly (Semester 4, once ACCTG 211/SCM 200/ECON 102 are satisfied). Adds 12cr beyond the bulletin's own stated total, documented rather than silently absorbed. Bumped max_credits_per_semester to 18 to keep the resulting load realistic given the additions.",
